# Everything here would either be rebuilt inside the image, break it, or leak
# something out of it. The build context is small on purpose: on a free tier the
# upload is a real part of every deploy's wall-clock time.

.git
.gitignore
.claude
README.md

# Rebuilt in the `web` stage. Copying a Windows-built dist in would ship
# whatever happened to be on the laptop rather than what the repo says.
frontend/dist
frontend/node_modules
frontend/.vite

# Chat history and the local SQLite file. The deployed app uses Postgres, and
# baking a database into an image would publish every local conversation.
backend/data

# A local virtualenv is Windows binaries; inside a Linux image it is worse than
# useless, because `pip install` would find it and skip work it must redo.
backend/.venv
.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.egg-info

# Secrets never enter the build context. Render supplies them as environment
# variables at runtime.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

.vscode
.idea
Thumbs.db

# Windows spouštěč. V Linuxovém image ho nic nespustí a .exe by jen zvětšilo
# upload build kontextu.
aplikace.exe
tools
